// pipeline.mn — the compiler's spine (spec 04 · 05 · 06 · 10)
//
// One file; five entry points; each a `|>` + `~>` topology. The `|>`
// chain IS the stages. The `~>` chain IS the capability stack —
// outermost least trusted, innermost most empowered. The shape of
// this file IS the compiler's architecture.
//
//   compile(src)  →  WAT bytes
//   check(src)    →  diagnostics (no lowering, no emit)
//   query(src,q)  →  structured answer
//   teach(src)    →  gradient recommendation
//   audit(src)    →  capability set + severance suggestions
//
// Each route shares the same substrate handlers — graph, env,
// diagnostics, lookup_ty_graph — and adds route-specific ones.
// Source is never re-inferred across routes; the graph is one.
//
// This file declares the handlers it OWNS:
//   lookup_ty_graph     — bridge GraphRead → LookupTy (spec 05)
//   diagnostics_handler — stderr diagnostic routing (spec 06)
// (env_handler lives at src/env.mn, the intern handlers at
//  src/intern.mn — the state's own modules, below infer.)
//
// Every other handler is imported from its owner module:
//   graph_handler       → graph.mn
//   verify_ledger       → verify.mn
//   mentl_default       → mentl.mn
//   query_default       → query.mn
//   affine_ledger       → own.mn
//   clock_real, tick_real, sample_real, deadline_real → clock.mn
import graph

import types

import effects

import env

import intern

import infer

import lower

import backends/wasm

import lexer

import parser

import own

import verify

import mentl

import query

import dsp/clock

import driver

import io

import egraph

// The spine — entry points as |> + ~> topology
// Read top-to-bottom: source flows DOWN through `|>`; handlers wrap
// OUTWARD through `~>`. Outermost handler is the sandbox boundary.
//
// THE ANALYSIS-CORE ORDER LAW (the one home — infer_context below is
// its single instantiation; every inference-reaching chain installs the
// bracket), inner to outer:
//
//   affine_ledger / region_tracker / verify_ledger — the analysis
//     ledgers, innermost: arms are pure state over the ops inference
//     performs (consume/borrow, region tags, proof debt).
//   lookup_ty_graph — the GraphRead → LookupTy bridge: its arms read
//     the graph, so graph_handler sits outer to it.
//   env_handler before graph_handler — env arms read the graph outer
//     to them.
//   graph_handler before mutate_sink — graph writes perform
//     graph_mutated, absorbed outward.
//   diagnostics_handler outer — graph_bind's occurs-check report
//     fires FROM a graph arm (graph.mn); the outer placement counts it
//     independent of dispatch tier.
//   intern_table OUTERMOST — the lex-name intern. It must sit OUTSIDE
//     diagnostics_handler because the report arm renders its message
//     live (diag_message → show_effrow → eff_name_str → intern_name_of),
//     and an arm's performs resolve OUTER to its own install (the
//     world-as-value R2 law) — an inner intern would leave the render
//     with no handler. Its own arms perform nothing but substrate ops,
//     so nothing needs to sit outside it; every identifier and every
//     EffName handle in the bracket resolves through this one instance,
//     and a nested bracket's own outermost intern keeps its isolation.
//
// The fn-shaped bracket was REFUTED once (2026-07-23, the mint-time
// evidence snapshot: a thunk's ops faulted where its creation site
// lacked installs) and became ADMISSIBLE the same night when the
// world-as-value arc's R2 made every evidence-tier perform resolve
// through the live install chain — a computation performs in the world
// where it is CALLED. The bracket is that arc's first wheel-internal
// consumer; the three mn-world-* frontier legs gate the semantics it
// rests on.
//
// The bracket takes the body as a thunk (the analyze_fns precedent);
// verb-specific handlers chain INSIDE the thunk, so their ops resolve
// innermost-first. NO schedule handler is here or at the dispatch
// boundary: the wheel's spine is sequential by artifact (a schedule
// installs lexically at the fanout it schedules — main.mn's dispatch
// comment carries the why). Nested installs stay isolating — a voice
// consult's compile_source brackets fresh instances inside a session's
// bracket (handler state is per-install).
//
// IC.4: compile / check route through driver_compile_entry /
// driver_entry_with_ranges when invoked with an entry-MODULE name;
// `driver_check` is the LSP and cursor transport's per-module walk
// (src/lsp.mn, src/cursor_transport.mn — a transport opens one
// document, not a weave). The
// single-source entry compile/check_source remain for tests that
// pass a raw source string. The
// driver path reads module sources via FS and infers each in
// dependency order; within-run incrementality IS the epoch cursor
// (§2 cached-cursor mode), and cross-run skip is the image-persist
// peer (Hβ.persist.module-image-cache).
fn infer_context(body) =
  body() ~> affine_ledger ~> region_tracker ~> verify_ledger ~> lookup_ty_graph ~> env_handler(make_list(0), 0, env_index_new()) ~> graph_handler([], 0, []) ~> mutate_sink ~> diagnostics_handler ~> intern_table

// The LOWERING/EMIT stack's one home — infer_context's peer on the far side
// of the cursor. Every route that lowers installs exactly this: string_table
// (compile-time interned string offsets), emit_memory_bump (the swap point
// for emit_memory_arena), mentl_default, lower_scope,
// lower_handler_stack_ctx (the lexical evidence fence's own stack),
// arm_state_ctx, spec_registry. A caller supplies only its SINK and its
// filesystem/persist prefix, because that is the only part that ever differs.
//
// It exists because its absence was already paid for: seven routes
// hand-copied this chain, `mentl march`'s copy omitted
// lower_handler_stack_ctx, and lower_frame_fence_push's perform hit the
// unhandled floor on every march the verb ran — the wheel unable to judge
// its own generation while tools/march.sh, which the board actually calls,
// stayed green. A chain with one home cannot lose a handler to a copy.
fn emit_context(body) =
  body() ~> string_table ~> emit_memory_bump ~> mentl_default ~> lower_scope ~> lower_handler_stack_ctx ~> arm_state_ctx([], OneShot, "") ~> spec_registry ~> emit_site_module

// A route that LOWERS installs both stacks, emit inside analysis, and that
// nesting order is itself a fact — so it has one home too rather than being
// re-derived at every lowering route. Analysis-only routes (check, query,
// the single-source check) keep infer_context alone; they have nothing to
// lower and installing an emit stack over them would be inert ceremony.
fn compile_context(body) = infer_context(() => emit_context(body))

// `driver_compile_entry` infers the deps DAG + the entry ONCE and returns
// the entry's already-typed AST — compile lowers that live graph, no
// second fs_read / re-judgment (Carried-Truth: the entry
// is proven once and read live, never re-derived).
fn compile(entry_module) = compile_context(() => entry_module |> driver_compile_entry |> compile_remainder ~>
// The emit SINK is the caller's install, never this chain's: compile_run
// streams to stdout (wat_stdout), run_run streams to the executor
// (wat_to_host) — one compile graph, the handler swap IS the verb. A sink
// baked in here would shadow every outer install and leave `run` unable to
// redirect its own product.
// the warm-start cache (driver_compile_entry)
persist_to_disk ~>
// image_resume's refusal policy (probe-guarded)
fail_exit ~>
// FS — per-file byte I/O for driver / cache
wasi_filesystem)

// Per Hβ.first-light.compile-stdin-substrate (2026-05-09): canonical
// stdin-source compile path. Per Unix vocabulary `mentl compile -`
// reads source from stdin. Skips driver_check + fs_read_file (no
// module-graph; no path); reads the entire stdin via read_stdin
// (lib/io.mn:83 — fd_read loop with grow-on-headroom buffer);
// pipes through frontend → lower_program → emit_module. Same handler
// chain as compile() — emission to stdout via wat_stdout, all the
// substrate handlers attached.
//
// L1 fixpoint requires this path: seed compiles wheel → mentl2.wat;
// mentl2 reads stdin (the wheel input) → emits mentl3.wat. Both passes
// produce byte-identical output when the wheel-source emit is
// deterministic AND substrate-aligned across seed + wheel.
// THE EXECUTABLE GATE (SYNTAX §«Partial application» — a hole is productive,
// never executable; §0's "nothing executes unproven" at its honest scope).
// Runs BETWEEN reachability and emit — wat_stdout streams every emit
// immediately, so the refusal must precede the first one; refusing here
// leaves stdout with ZERO WAT bytes. Two reads, one law each:
//   HOLES REFUSE. An authored value-position hole surviving in the
//   reachable set (the value-holes COLUMN read — call-arg holes became
//   partial params, pipe holes were spliced/unnoted, so survival IS
//   value-position; a dead entry's hole pairs with an unreached name
//   and never refuses) reports
//   E_UnresolvedHole at its authored span and the compile exits 1 —
//   diagnostics on stderr, no module. Typed absence is not a value.
//   HONEST DEBT SURFACES — and compiles. V_Pending is the sound-incomplete
//   NORMAL state (§4/§5: undecidable residue accrues, never assume-true);
//   the wheel's own self-compile carries obligations that are structurally
//   undecidable without the SMT handler swap, so refusing on pending would
//   refuse the medium itself (the fleet's measured refutation of the
//   blanket form). The ledger projects one summary diagnostic; the
//   per-entry projections stay query/edit surfaces.
// `check` never routes here — the productive surfaces admit holes; only an
// EXECUTABLE refuses to exist around one.
// gate_reads — the gate LAW's judge half, one home for its three policies:
// executable_gate (refuse + proc_exit — the CLI compile, one process one
// verdict), battery_compile (batch: count and continue), and the mcp
// judge (serve: verdict as data, the server outlives every refusal). The
// reports land before the diag_refusals read — the teaching precedes the
// tally it feeds.
fn gate_reads(lowered) = {
  report_verify_debt(verify_debt())
  report_unhandled_effects(lowered)
  let holes = column_value_holes(lowered)
  // The ARMED classes, read LIVE off the ledger the diagnostics handler keeps
  // (diag_refuses names them; a class arms only when the wheel's own census of it
  // is zero, so this can never refuse the medium). The hole gate was this law
  // with one arm; these are its others. Productive at the walk, refusing at the
  // boundary — SYNTAX's "a hole is productive, never executable", generalized.
  //
  // The verdict binds BEFORE the hole report so refusals never double-count
  // a hole (report_holes raises the armed E_UnresolvedHole; the tally read
  // above deliberately precedes it — len(holes) is the hole half).
  let refused = diag_refusals()
  let nholes = len(holes)
  let verdict = (nholes, refused)
  if nholes > 0 { report_holes(holes, 0) }
  verdict
}

fn executable_gate(lowered) = match gate_reads(lowered) {
  (nholes, refused) => if nholes == 0 && refused == 0 {
    lowered
  } else {
    if refused > 0 {
      eprint_string("mentl: refusing to emit — {int_to_str(refused)} claim(s) the medium could not discharge\n")
    }
    proc_exit(1)
    // proc_exit never returns (the emit appends unreachable after it);
    // the tail value only closes the type of the branch.
    lowered
  },
}

// ─── The evidence hole — the gate's third read ──────────────────────
// An executable's row truth at the root: main's resolved row carries every
// effect no install absorbed. The triple representation carries the `~>`
// subtraction on the tail's mask, so this row is TRUE — a rewrite-based
// representation lied here (an install typed before its body's row grounded
// never subtracted, the fat-row root the ledger records), which is why this
// read requires the triple. A
// present name whose ops the substrate does not project to instructions is
// an EVIDENCE HOLE: some perform of it would key-scan a region no install
// threaded — the 0x100000000 class, refused at compile with the
// graph-derived proposal instead of discovered as a memory fault at
// runtime. Compiler attributions (GraphRead, Consume — row FACTS with no
// declared ops) and the substrate effects (Memory/Alloc/the WASI set —
// every op an instruction projection) ground vacuously; only an
// evidence-dispatched family refuses. check/edit never route here — the
// productive surfaces stay open (SYNTAX: a hole is productive, never
// executable — this is the same law at the evidence altitude).
fn report_unhandled_effects(lowered) = match env_lookup("main") {
  Some(entry) => match entry {
    (scheme, reason, _) => match judgment_ty(scheme) {
      TFun{row} => match resolve_row(row) {
        EfRow{present: p} => {
          // The evidence census — the emit's OWN single-walk projection
          // (the seventh: visit_effect_demand/install), run over the
          // post-reach tree the gate already holds. The artifact is the
          // truth source: dead-code performs never appear (reach pruned
          // them from this tree), and every perform that WALKS carries its
          // ename in its own dispatch, so the demand is read off the node
          // rather than re-derived. The full collector bracket rides along because the one
          // walk fires every projection's ops.
          let census = {
            walk_lemit(lowered)
            drain_effect_census()
          } ~> effect_census_collector ~> fn_names_collector ~> top_fn_names_collector ~> string_literal_collector ~> state_slots_collector ~> yield_seen_collector ~> wasi_ops_collector
          match census {
            (demands, installed) => report_unhandled_names(
              p,
              0,
              len(p),
              demands_to_enames(demands, 0, []),
              installed,
              reason_span_or_zero(reason)
            ),
          }
        },
      },
      _ => (),
    },
  },
  None => (),
}

// A drained demand is an ename already (the floor's ekey) or a yield's
// OP name — resolve ops to their effect through the live scheme; a name
// that is no op passes through as itself. That is the WHOLE job.
//
// THE THREE TIERS ARE DELETED, and they were one question the substrate no
// longer asks. Each tier was a soundness story about how a perform reaches
// its handler: a STATELESS singleton "grounded" because a chainless direct
// call ignores __state; a STATEFUL singleton cleared on an install anywhere
// because a direct call needed a record the chain might supply; an
// EVIDENCE-floor demand was strict because it alone walked. Every one of
// those distinctions described the dispatch TIER, and there are no tiers —
// one walk, one refusal, the same belt under all of them. What remained was
// handler_stateful, whose only other reader built a `DtSingleton` Bool that
// nothing ever read.
//
// The licence the stateless tier carried is what let a handler's own arms
// escape unnoticed: `format_default` re-emits `Format`, so `Format` survives
// to main's root row (measured — a declared `!Render` on the same shape
// refuses with `Memory + Alloc + Render`), and the gate dropped the demand
// before it could be seen. The ROW is authoritative and always was.
fn demands_to_enames(ref demands, i, acc) = if i >= len(demands) {
  acc
} else {
  let d = list_index(demands, i)
  let en = match env_lookup(d) {
    Some(entry) => match entry {
      (_, _, kind) => match kind {
        EffectOpScheme{effect_name: op_effect} => op_effect,
        _ => d,
      },
    },
    None => d,
  }
  demands_to_enames(demands, i + 1, if string_in_list(acc, en) { acc } else { push(acc, en) })
}

fn report_unhandled_names(ref names, i, n, ref performed, ref installed, ref span) = if i >= n {
  ()
} else {
  let ename = eff_name_str(list_index(names, i))
  // TWO CONJUNCTS, because the row is authoritative: the effect is PRESENT
  // at the executable root (this list IS main's residual row — everything
  // any `~>` absorbed has already been subtracted), it is not
  // SUBSTRATE-GROUNDED, and it is actually PERFORMED somewhere reachable.
  // The last one is the only thing the emit census is for and it is real: a
  // declared-but-never-performed row (`with Sample`, SYNTAX's own lowpass)
  // is the iterative-class canon, never an evidence hole.
  //
  // AND the `installed` licence, which survives BY MEASUREMENT after being
  // deleted and refuted in one build. Deleting it looked right — the row is
  // authoritative, and a per-candidate `~>` is lexically present where it
  // runs — but the wheel refused on `GraphRead`: `graph_handler`'s arms
  // perform sibling GraphRead ops, and that is legal FORWARDING, because the
  // wheel NESTS graph installs (dispatch_invocation installs one, each
  // compile installs another that shadows it), so an inner arm's sibling
  // perform reaches the outer handler. The row cannot see that nesting — it
  // is a whole-program fact about install identity, which is band A's seat
  // exactly as this file already said. So an install anywhere still clears.
  //
  // What that licence therefore CANNOT catch is the same shape with no outer
  // install: `format_default` re-emits `Format` from its own arm, reaching
  // the root, cleared because format_default is "installed somewhere" — it
  // compiled clean and trapped in `mentl fmt`. That gap is real and named
  // (Hβ.effects.handler-re-emits-what-it-handles); the decl-site narration
  // below is what makes it visible today, and band A is what refuses it.
  if effect_ops_substrate_grounded(ename) {
    ()
  } else if !string_in_list(performed, ename) {
    ()
  } else if string_in_list(installed, ename) {
    ()
  } else {
    // Sequenced effectful read BEFORE the construction (the record-
    // construction exception): the proposal's env scan performs, and a
    // ctor argument list is not the place for a perform.
    let proposal = absorbing_proposal(ename)
    report(EEffectUnhandled(ename, proposal, span))
  }
  report_unhandled_names(names, i + 1, n, performed, installed, span)
}

// Every op of the effect projects to a substrate instruction (the
// Memory/Alloc table, the WASI import set) — or the name owns no ops at
// all (a compiler attribution: a row fact, never an evidence dispatch).
fn effect_ops_substrate_grounded(ename: String) = match env_snapshot() {
  Env(bindings) => grounded_scan(bindings, 0, len(bindings), ename),
}

fn grounded_scan(ref bindings, i, n, ename: String) = if i >= n {
  true
} else {
  match list_index(bindings, i) {
    (opname, _, _, kind) => {
      let ok = match kind {
        EffectOpScheme{effect_name: op_effect} => // Substrate projection or WASI import only. A DEFAULT HANDLER does
        // NOT ground: the perform's singleton tier direct-calls it, but a
        // STATEFUL default with no live install reads its zero state
        // global — the silent-wrong the runtime guard refuses
        // (SingletonUninstalled; in the retired keyed-evidence era the
        // same shape broke at assembly, the sst build's ev_lookup).
        // The intrinsic families (to_string/hash) never reach the perform
        // dispatch, so they ground through the not-performed conjunct,
        // never through a default field.
        if op_effect == ename { is_substrate_mem_op(opname) || is_wasi_import_op(opname) } else { true },
        _ => true,
      }
      if ok { grounded_scan(bindings, i + 1, n, ename) } else { false }
    },
  }
}

// The teaching half: which declared handlers absorb this effect — read
// from the env's own HandlerKind arms (each arm's op resolves to its
// effect through the op scheme), never a name table. No handler in scope
// teaches the declare-one form.
fn absorbing_proposal(ename: String) = {
  let hs = handlers_absorbing(ename)
  if len(hs) == 0 {
    "No handler in scope handles {ename} — declare one and install it with ~> over the performing chain."
  } else {
    let rendered = show_list(hs, render_install, " or ")
    "Install one over the performing chain: {rendered}."
  }
}

fn render_install(ref hname: String) = "~> {hname}"

fn handlers_absorbing(ename: String) = match env_snapshot() {
  Env(bindings) => absorb_scan(bindings, 0, len(bindings), ename, []),
}

fn absorb_scan(ref bindings, i, n, ename: String, own acc) = if i >= n {
  acc
} else {
  match list_index(bindings, i) {
    (hname, _, _, kind) => {
      let hit = match kind {
        HandlerKind(_, _, _, arms) => handler_arms_touch(arms, 0, len(arms), ename),
        _ => false,
      }
      // The flat env carries a handler at several layers (pre_register + the
      // main walk); the proposal names each handler once.
      if hit && !string_in_list(acc, hname) {
        absorb_scan(bindings, i + 1, n, ename, push(acc, hname))
      } else {
        absorb_scan(bindings, i + 1, n, ename, acc)
      }
    },
  }
}

fn handler_arms_touch(ref arms: [{args: [String], body: Node, op_name: String}], i, n, ename: String) = if i >= n {
  false
} else {
  // The receiver is ANNOTATED, which is what makes the destructure below
  // provable rather than promised. Field offsets resolve from the
  // receiver's full sorted field set; an OPEN row has no such set, so
  // lowering falls back to the pattern's own index — right only if the
  // pattern happens to name every field of the record that actually
  // arrives. The comment here used to say a full pattern "pins the
  // record's real layout", and it does not: a complete pattern over an
  // open row and a partial one are structurally IDENTICAL to the medium
  // (both leave known-fields = the pattern's fields, plus an open tail),
  // so the discipline was an author's promise the graph could not check.
  // The annotation closes the row, and the offsets become a proof.
  // `Hβ.lower.record-pattern-param-receiver` carries the class.
  match list_index(arms, i) {
    {args: _, body: _, op_name: opn} => {
      let touches = match env_lookup(opn) {
        Some(op_entry) => match op_entry {
          (_, _, op_kind) => match op_kind {
            EffectOpScheme{effect_name: op_effect} => op_effect == ename,
            _ => false,
          },
        },
        None => false,
      }
      if touches { true } else { handler_arms_touch(arms, i + 1, n, ename) }
    },
  }
}

fn report_holes(holes, i) = if i >= len(holes) {
  ()
} else {
  let h = list_index(holes, i)
  // The weave span — the parse truth authored_hole itself proved; the
  // reason-chain span is clobbered by the binder's unification.
  report_at(h, EUnresolvedHole(h, parse_span_of(h)))
  report_holes(holes, i + 1)
}

// The compile's projection half — everything after the analyzed graph.
// ONE home: the cold path, the warm path, and the resume verb all run
// exactly this remainder over their ast (the persisted image's typed
// root included), so the three routes cannot drift.
fn compile_remainder(ast) =
  ast |> saturate_pass |> lower_program |> reachable_from_main |> executable_gate |> emit_module

// `mentl resume <img>` — the image IS the process: swap it in and run
// the compile remainder over the restored typed root, the source not
// required to exist (the projection rode the image — the absence is the
// proof). The chain mirrors compile's: the pre-swap fs/fail ops resolve
// through it, the executable gate's static demands ground in it, and
// every post-swap dispatch walks the RESTORED world regardless.
fn resume_image(img_path) = compile_context(() => {
  eprint_string("warm: restoring the persisted image\n")
  image_resume(img_path)
  compile_remainder(warm_program())
} ~> wat_stdout ~> persist_to_disk ~> fail_exit ~> wasi_filesystem)

fn compile_stdin() =
  compile_context(() => read_stdin() |> infer_program_converged |> compile_remainder ~> wat_stdout ~> wasi_filesystem)

// pipeline_check returns its own ERROR COUNT, because it owns the handler that
// does the counting (the diagnostics_handler at the foot of this chain).
//
// The read has to live HERE, and finding that out cost a build: check_run tried
// to read diag_errors() from its own outer install and always got 0. That is
// innermost-wins working exactly as documented — every report performed inside
// this chain is caught by THIS handler, so the outer one never sees them and its
// tally is honestly zero. The count and the counter are one handler; a reader
// outside the install is reading a different ledger.
//
// Check runs the same analyses as compile — the region-op and null-page
// classes this chain paid for (the zero-state sentinel reads, the
// SingletonUninstalled catches) are why EVERY inference-reaching chain
// installs the whole core; infer_context is that law as one home.
fn pipeline_check(entry_module) = infer_context(() => {
  // Check reads the SAME one-namespace weave every other driver verb
  // reads (compile / at / edit — driver_entry_with_ranges): whole-program
  // truth, one span space. The old per-module walk (driver_check) inferred
  // each module against only the layers already installed, so prelude's
  // own body missed the substrate vocabulary its layer supplies —
  // E_MissingVariable noise on a clean program. The per-module env
  // overlay (Hβ.driver.per-module-env-overlay) is that walk's sequenced
  // refinement; until it lands, the weave IS the check.
  driver_entry_with_ranges(entry_module)
  diag_errors()
} ~> wasi_filesystem ~> mentl_default)

// Legacy single-source entry — for tests that pass raw source
// without filesystem layout. No caching; full re-infer each call.
fn compile_source(source) =
  compile_context(() => source |> infer_program_converged |> compile_remainder ~> wat_stdout)

fn check_source(source) = infer_context(() => source |> infer_program_converged ~> mentl_default)

// entry_ast — the judged source AT AN ADDRESS, whatever the address names.
// `Some(ast)` when the address produced readable source; `None` when it did
// not, which the caller refuses rather than answering over an empty weave.
//
// `-` IS AN ADDRESS. It names stdin — the bare compile's own path, a
// self-contained source with no weave to derive — and the two-line arm that
// says so lived inside `analyze_fns` alone until 2026-09-21, so `audit` and
// `teach` could read stdin while `query` and `check` answered *"module source
// not found: - (expected at lib/-.mn)"*. One fact, one home, and the readers
// that did not share it were the ones that could not ask the blob link a
// question at all — which is how this was found: a probe on the wheel's own
// link divergence had nowhere to run.
//
// Anything else derives THE WEAVE — the same `driver_entry_with_ranges` the
// check verb, the address, `fmt` and the resident session read. A SECOND
// discovery route is what that replaced, and what it cost is why there is
// exactly one: a module judged SOLO is judged without its layer's vocabulary
// (the per-module-env-overlay residue), flooding `E_MissingVariable` on
// `True`/`len` from any out-of-tree directory.
fn entry_ast(entry_module) = if entry_module == "-" {
  Some(read_stdin() |> infer_program_converged)
} else {
  match driver_entry_with_ranges(entry_module) {
    (ast_all, ranges) => match range_of_module(ranges, entry_module) {
      None => None,
      Some(_) => Some(driver_module_ast(ast_all, entry_module)),
    },
  }
}

// The shared refusal: an address that produced no source refuses the question
// itself rather than answering over an empty weave (the silent-fallback class
// — the census once printed "0 sites" for a file the judge could not read).
// Productive-under-error stays for JUDGED files.
fn refuse_unreadable(entry_module) with WASI + Memory + Alloc = {
  eprint_string("mentl: no source to project — {entry_module} never joined the weave\n")
  1
}

// COLD by the swap-crossing law (Hβ.session.resident-verbs — the
// measured refutation is in the §7 ledger): a mid-verb image restore
// kills every pre-swap heap value — the caller's own argv strings,
// the chain's own handler records — and survives only by allocation
// coincidence. The warm form for the projection verbs is the
// RESIDENT SESSION (the image as the session's own memory, no swap —
// the named peer carries the measured constraints); fresh derivation
// here IS the sound form for a per-process verb.
// `entry_ast` is the ONE discovery home — the weave for a module, stdin
// for `-`, and the same refusal for an address that produced neither.
fn query(entry_module, words) = infer_context(() => match entry_ast(entry_module) {
  None => refuse_unreadable(entry_module),
  Some(_) => {
    let q = parse_query_words(words)
    ask(q) |> render_query_result |> println
    0
  },
} ~>
// the derivation's fs_read — handled in-chain, as compile/check do
wasi_filesystem ~> query_default ~> mentl_default ~> arm_state_ctx([], OneShot, "") ~> spec_registry)

// ─── The tightening bank — T_OverDeclared as a live frontier fact ────
//
// T_OverDeclared already IS a proposal (the diagnostic carries the
// declared row, the proven body row, the fn name, and the decl span,
// MachineApplicable); this collector banks each one as the judgment
// fires it, so the tighten verb AND the frontier field read the same
// candidates live. tighten_reset clears the bank at a generation
// boundary — the living session re-derives on a moved tree, and stale
// generations' candidates must not shadow the current truth.
effect Tighten {
  // the MODULE rides each candidate: `mentl tighten` edits a FILE, and a
  // local span names a line without naming which file's line it is.
  tightenables() -> [(EffRow, EffRow, String, Span, String)]
  tighten_reset()
}

// The collecting forwarder over the Diag effect: TOverDeclared
// accumulates in state AND every diagnostic re-performs outward from the
// arm — sound because an arm's own performs resolve in the INSTALL's
// world (the world arc's deep-handler law), reaching the bracket's
// diagnostics_handler, never re-entering this collector. All three Diag
// ops carry arms: a handler arming only SOME ops of an effect leaves
// zero fn slots for the rest, and a perform through a zero slot is a
// garbage dispatch.
handler tighten_collector with found = [] {
  diag_report(diag, line, dmod) => {
    // Forward outward with the SAME rendered line — the forwarder never
    // re-renders (the line was made once, at the report boundary), and the
    // module rides along unread: a forwarder must not re-derive what the
    // reporter already established.
    diag_report(diag, line, dmod)
    match diag {
      TOverDeclared(declared, used, name, span) => resume() with found = push(found, (declared, used, name, span, dmod)),
      _ => resume(),
    }
  },
  diag_errors() => resume(diag_errors()),
  diag_refusals() => resume(diag_refusals()),
  tightenables() => resume(found),
  tighten_reset() => resume() with found = [],
}

// analyze_fns — the shared analysis-verb cursor: load+check the module,
// run one composed `projection(ast) -> String`, print. audit and teach
// ARE this cursor at two projections — the check handler chain and the
// load → project → print skeleton lived twice, byte-identical but for
// the projection (Carried-Truth: one home now). query stays separate:
// it ASKS a question, not a per-fn walk.
//
// `entry_ast` is the ONE discovery home (its own comment carries why
// there is exactly one, and why `-` is an address). This verb held that
// arm alone and so was the only surface stdin could reach; it reads the
// shared one now — and gains the refusal it never had, where an
// unreadable address used to project an empty walk as though it were an
// answer.
fn analyze_fns(entry_module, projection) = infer_context(() => match entry_ast(entry_module) {
  None => refuse_unreadable(entry_module),
  Some(ast) => {
    projection(ast) |> print_string
    0
  },
} ~>
// The weave's own fs_read — handled in-chain, as compile/check do.
// tighten_collector banks the judgment's T_OverDeclared rows so the
// audit projection can speak them per decl — the collector sits INSIDE
// the infer_context body chain, where the judgment's performs reach it.
wasi_filesystem ~> mentl_default ~> arm_state_ctx([], OneShot, "") ~> spec_registry ~> tighten_collector)

// The pure projection pair — audit and teach as `ast -> String`, the ONE
// home the CLI verb and the resident session's tool both call (the
// address_project law at the analysis verbs): the CLI derives an ast
// then projects; the session projects the living ast it already holds.
// Transport stays the caller's — analyze_fns prints, the session banks.
fn teach_project(ast) =
  map_fn_stmts(ast, (name, handle) => (name, teach_gradient(handle))) |> render_gradients

// The banks the judgment already holds, read ONCE and attributed per
// fn: pending proof obligations by decl EXTENT — this decl's span start
// to the next decl's, parse_span_of being the O(1) spans-column read —
// and tightenings by the name the collector banked. The audit and the
// frontier are two projections of the same banks; this read keeps the
// per-fn surface current with the medium's growth.
fn audit_project(ast) =
  map_fn_stmts(ast, (name, handle) => (name, handle)) |> audit_walk(verify_debt(), tightenables(), 0) |> render_audit

fn decl_start_line(handle) with GraphRead = match parse_span_of(handle) {
  Span{start_line: sl} => sl,
}

fn audit_walk(debt, tights, i, fns) with GraphRead + EnvRead + LookupTy + Memory + Alloc + Intern + WASI = if i >= len(fns) {
  []
} else {
  match fns[i] {
    (name, handle) => {
      // The next decl's handle by destructure — the index sugar forces
      // its receiver to List, so tuple[k] on a var receiver mis-judges
      // (SYNTAX's tuple-index claim vs the judge: a named lathe-lag).
      let extent_end = if i + 1 >= len(fns) {
        1000000000
      } else {
        match fns[i + 1] {
          (_, nh) => decl_start_line(nh),
        }
      }
      let extent = Span(decl_start_line(handle), 0, extent_end, 0)
      let pending = filter({ (_modh, dspan, _, _) => span_overlaps(extent, dspan) }, debt)
      let mine = filter({ (_, _, tname, _, _) => tname == name }, tights)
      [build_audit_report(name, handle, lookup_ty(handle), pending, mine)] ++ audit_walk(debt, tights, i + 1, fns)
    },
  }
}

fn teach(entry_module) = analyze_fns(entry_module, teach_project)

fn audit(entry_module) = analyze_fns(entry_module, audit_project)

// ─── Multi-module compilation — map over a module list ──────────────
//
// compile_pair_modules (binary special-case) was erased per
// CLAUDE.md Anchor 6: the driver's topological-layer walk
// (`Hβ.driver.level-set-par-walk`, layer partition live in driver.mn)
// composes each dep-independent layer as `map(compile, layer)`; the
// multi-core half is a `><` fanout under `~> Thread` at the layer
// site (Hβ.lower.schedule-specialized-callee). Render targets attach
// via `~>` to the per-module wat output. Drift 6 erasure.
//
// THE DEAD ROOT OF THE RANKED-QUEUE ORACLE WAS HERE, and its sentence was
// the tell: "`mentl edit` IS this loop running." It was not. The decl —
// ic_compile_loop, unbackticked because it no longer resolves — had ZERO
// callers, measured by `mentl src/main.mn unreachable` which named it
// before anything else did; and `mentl edit` routes through `edit_run` / `mentl_edit_session`,
// nowhere near it. It was also the ONLY install site of the queue merger, so
// an entire subsystem hung off a function nobody called: 25 decls in
// src/oracle.mn (the priority-queue machine — project_queue, compute_priority,
// the priority_* / tier_* orders, sort_by_priority, merge_by_impact, the
// filter_by_* family, handle_distance) and 9 in voice, all unreachable. None
// of those names is backticked: the module is deleted and they resolve
// nowhere, which is the difference between prose and a reference.
//
// The subsystem it rooted is SUPERSEDED, not merely unused: PLAN §11.1
// re-founded the oracle as inference with a term-sorted unknown — propagation
// before enumeration, forking only at genuine disjunction — and a project-wide
// queue that re-runs the proposer at every position and sorts by a hand-tuned
// intent × surface-area × locality priority is exactly the generate-then-filter
// shape that re-founding names and refutes. The LIVE ranked absence field is
// the frontier (`mentl <file>:0`). Two homes for one projection, and the dead
// one was the superseded design. `Hβ.oracle.ranked-queue-is-a-second-frontier`
// carries the deletion of the rest.
//
// One thing that deletion answered, measured at the moment the root went and
// recorded before the rest followed it: with the root gone the queue merger
// had NO install site anywhere, `mentl src/main.mn check` still passed, and
// `silence_predicate` (src/voice.mn) — reachable, called from a handler arm —
// still performed query_project_queue. A reachable perform with zero handlers
// compiles clean. `Hβ.effects.reachable-perform-with-no-install-compiles`
// carries it; the predicate reads the gradient field now, so the wheel no
// longer contains that shape, and the GATE that let it through still does.
//
// The env substrate — buffer, index, resolve, dedup, and env_handler —
// lives in src/env.mn now (PLAN §11 Phase 3.5, the handler seam: the
// install chain in infer names the handler, so the declaration lives
// below infer at the state's own module). The intern handlers moved to
// src/intern.mn the same day for the same seam. This module imports
// both; the compile chains install them exactly as before.
// ── (relocated) O(1) env resolution — the str_hash-bucket index ─────────────
// wasi_filesystem — FS substrate (IC prerequisite)
// Four-arm stateless handler delegating to io.mn primitives.
// Grants Filesystem capability to the driver's module reads. Installed in
// `compile`'s ~> chain between wat_stdout and the compiler-internal
// handlers — fs stays a driver-level capability, not something the
// compiler's own code accidentally reaches for.
//
// Audit implications: a function that doesn't reach fs_* ops proves
// `with !Filesystem`; audit-driven linker severance drops path_open
// / fd_close / path_create_directory / path_filestat_get imports
// from that binary. PLAN §0's capability severance, realized.
handler wasi_filesystem {
  fs_exists(path) => resume(fs_exists_impl(path)),
  fs_read_file(path) => resume(fs_read_file_impl(path)),
  fs_write_file(path, bytes) => {
    fs_write_file_impl(path, bytes)
    resume()
  },
  fs_mkdir(path) => {
    fs_mkdir_impl(path)
    resume()
  },
  fs_open(path) => // FX.A.basics arms (per FX walkthrough §2.2)
  resume(fs_open_impl(path)),
  fs_create(path) => resume(fs_create_impl(path)),
  fs_close(fd) => {
    fs_close_impl(fd)
    resume()
  },
  fs_unlink(path) => resume(fs_unlink_impl(path)),
  fs_rename(old_p, new_p) => resume(fs_rename_impl(old_p, new_p)),
}

// lookup_ty_graph (the GraphRead → LookupTy bridge, with the
// specialization state) lives in graph.mn — the projection reads
// graph_chase, and the branch bracket (infer.mn) installs it, so the
// graph is the one home both import.
//
// diag_line lives beside diag_message in types.mn now — the render moved
// to the report BOUNDARY (the report fn), so the arms below receive the
// finished line and never render.
//
// diagnostics_handler — stderr routing (spec 06)
// The sandbox boundary. Outermost in every route. Declares
// `with !Diagnostic` so its own arms cannot recursively perform
// report — structural gate via spec 01's algebra.
handler diagnostics_handler with errors = 0, refusals = 0, scope = ScopeAll {
  diag_report(diag, line, dmod) => // The line arrives MADE (rendered at the report boundary, in the
  // reporter's own world) — this arm's remaining projections
  // (severity, refuses, span, the register's file-local rewrite) are
  // pure ctor/string reads, so the arm's row carries no graph or
  // intern demand and its residual stays clean through every install.
  // The tally IS the projection continued. This arm saw every diagnostic and
  // dropped its severity on the floor, so `mentl check` on a missing module
  // printed the error and exited 0, and a program with a live E_TypeMismatch
  // emitted 77 lines of WAT. The verdict was here the whole time; the exit
  // code re-derived it as success.
  if diag_severity(diag) == SError {
    // An error renders in EVERY scope — a broken claim anywhere in the
    // weave changes the answer's validity; the register never silences it.
    eprint_string(line)
    if diag_refuses(diag) {
      resume() with errors = errors + 1, refusals = refusals + 1
    } else {
      resume() with errors = errors + 1
    }
  } else {
    // Narration is the register's business: ScopeAll (the census paths)
    // prints everything; ScopeModule renders only the file the user asked
    // about. The comparison is on the module the report CARRIES, not on a
    // line range — spans are local now, so every file starts at line 1 and a
    // range names nothing.
    match scope {
      ScopeAll => eprint_string(line),
      ScopeNone => (),
      ScopeModule(target) => if dmod == target { eprint_string(line) } else { () },
    }
    resume()
  },
  diag_errors() => resume(errors),
  diag_refusals() => resume(refusals),
  diag_scope(sc) => resume() with scope = sc,
  diag_scope_of() => resume(scope),
}

// scope_localize DELETED with the weave: it rebuilt every rendered span by
// subtracting the module's weave offset back off it, string-slicing the `at
// <span>` tail and re-rendering the arithmetic. Spans are local from birth,
// so the number it computed is now the number the span already holds.
//
// diag_branch (the branch cursor's per-stmt collector) lives in
// infer.mn beside diag_quiet — the branch bracket and the join are its
// only consumers.
//
// FreshHandle — two handlers, same function. Inference mints via
// graph_fresh_ty (stored in graph) — that handler lives in infer.mn, its
// op's own layer, so synth's re-inference chain reaches it through
// `import infer` (the import-truth round: pipeline was an over-wide home
// only its own chain could see). Query mints display ids (ephemeral, for
// rendering); both satisfy FreshHandle.
handler fresh_for_query with next_display = 0 {
  mint(_reason) => resume(next_display) with next_display = next_display + 1,
  mint_row(_reason) => resume(next_display) with next_display = next_display + 1,
}

// Collection helpers — consumed by teach / audit
//
// Per-fn gradient projection. Each FnStmt's teach_gradient is
// independent of siblings (no shared state mutation among reads);
// map's tail loop walks them. N-core gradients are a `><` under its
// own `~> Thread` at this site (Hβ.lower.schedule-specialized-callee).
// map_fn_stmts — project every top-level FnStmt to `project(name, handle)`,
// dropping non-fn nodes. The ONE cursor walk over the module's fn decls;
// audit and teach are two projections of it (Carried-Truth: the walk lived
// twice, byte-identical but for the projection — one home now).
fn map_fn_stmts(ast, project) = ast |> map({
  N{body, handle} => match body {
    NStmt(FnStmt{name}) => [project(name, handle)],
    _ => [],
  },
}) |> flatten

// The element pin is an Intent Boundary (spec_mangle's law): name's
// only use is the splice, so unpinned the fn generalizes and the floor
// renders every fn's teach line under a pointer numeral instead of its
// name.
fn render_gradients(gradients: [(String, Option(AnnotationSuggestion))]) = if len(gradients) == 0 {
  "All functions are at maximum annotation density.\n"
} else {
  gradients |> map({ (name, result) => render_gradient_line(name, result) }) |> str_concat_all
}

// The name pin is an Intent Boundary at the line's ONE mint (spec_mangle's
// law): inside the map lambda the splice judged datum-last while the
// element was still free, and the show floor read the word — every teach
// line rendered under a pointer numeral. The named call anchors the
// binder to String before the splice judges.
fn render_gradient_line(name: String, result) = "{name}: {render_gradient_result(result)}\n"

fn render_gradient_result(result) = match result {
  None => "(no next-step annotation suggested)",
  Some(suggestion) => match suggestion {
    AnnotationSuggestion(_kind, ann_text, unlocks, _reason) => "→ add {ann_text} to unlock {join_unlock_labels(unlocks)}",
  },
}

fn join_unlock_labels(labels) with Memory + Alloc = if len(labels) == 0 {
  "(no capabilities)"
} else {
  let first = head(labels)
  let rest = rest(labels)
  fold(first, (acc, label) => acc ++ ", " ++ label, rest)
}

// H5: AuditReport record per fn — the structured projection Mentl's
// IDE surfaces (Proof Lens, Gradient ghost text, JSON export). Each
// field is independently introspectable; the record shape lets new
// metadata land additively (per CLAUDE.md insight 9).
//
// Fields:
//   fn_name        — the function's identifier
//   row_str        — pre-rendered row for terminal output
//   severable_all  — every effect NOT in the body, provable as `!E`
//                    ([EffName]). The named subset, its unlocks and the
//                    unnamed remainder are FOLDS of this list, asked at the
//                    render where the module's own severance is subtracted
//                    first — `audit_severable` is the one accessor.
//
// A TUPLE, not a record: render_audit reads these fields inside a map
// lambda, and a structural record's fields floor "field offset
// unprovable" there (map's lambda param doesn't inherit the list element
// type, and the wheel lowers no nominal record PATTERN to prove it — §7
// field-offset class). Positional destructure is provable with no type
// flow, exactly as teach's [(name, result)] tuples are.
fn build_audit_report(fn_name, handle, ty, pending, tightens) = {
  // The row resolves BEFORE any read: row_names is a top-link read, and
  // an unchased chain hides its deeper presents — Alloc rendered in the
  // row while severance claimed it absent (measured on the wheel's own
  // audit). One chased value serves the render and the membership.
  let body_row = chase_row_deep(extract_row(ty), 0)
  let reached = row_names(body_row)
  // THE GRADIENT, not the flood: every declared-but-unreached effect is
  // provably severable, but the ones that TEACH are those whose absence
  // unlocks a named capability — those lead the line; the rest ride as a
  // count (true, and honest about carrying no teaching yet). A constant
  // three-name line was what the hardcoded vocabulary could say; this is
  // the read ranked by what it buys.
  // The entry carries the CANDIDATES and nothing derived from them. The
  // named subset, its unlocks and the unnamed remainder's count were three
  // fields here, each a fold over this one list, each re-read at the render
  // that could have folded it — Carried-Truth inside the verb that projects
  // it. One list; `severance_named` / `severance_unlocks` / `len` answer the
  // three questions where they are asked.
  let severable_all = severance_candidates(reached)
  // The comment-reference edges' reverse read: which comments point here.
  let referenced_by = graph_comment_refs_of(handle) |> map(comment_owner)
  // The verb-shape read (oracle's pipe_shape_of): single-use let-chains
  // that already draw a `|>` — the topology tier of the audit. Beside it
  // the iteration-shape read (recursion_shape_of): a self-call threading
  // an incremented index is the loop in recursion's costume — iteration
  // is topology (|> stages, <~ cycles, derived folds), and the audit
  // names the costume where it stands.
  (fn_name, show_effrow(body_row), severable_all, referenced_by, pipe_shape_of(handle), recursion_shape_of(handle), anonymity_shape_of(handle), drift_shapes_of(handle), pending, tightens)
}

// The severable candidates a report entry carries — the one field every
// severance question folds, named so the ten-wide destructure has one home.
fn audit_severable(entry) = match entry {
  (_, _, sev, _, _, _, _, _, _, _) => sev,
}

// THE SEVERANCE OF A MODULE — the fact at the widest node that proves it.
//
// An effect is severable module-wide exactly when NO function in the module
// reaches it, which is the INTERSECTION of the functions' own candidates. It
// was rendered per function instead, and the wheel measured what that costs:
// `mentl src/main.mn audit` printed 303 lines of which 122 were `severable:`
// lines carrying exactly TWO distinct facts — 98 saying `Network`, 24 saying
// `Network + Alloc` — because nothing in the module performs Network and the
// module-level truth was re-derived and re-printed once per function. Forty
// percent of a projection spent restating one edge, burying the 55 lines that
// were findings.
//
// So the module's severance is read ONCE here, and a function's own line
// carries only what the module's fact does not already prove. A developer
// reading `severs module-wide: Network` learns the whole module is
// sandboxable — which 98 repetitions of that sentence actively hid.
fn module_severance(entries) with Memory + Alloc = match entries {
  [] => [],
  [first, ...more] => more |> fold(audit_severable(first), intersect_severance),
}

fn intersect_severance(acc, entry) with Memory + Alloc =
  acc |> filter({ e => name_in_list(audit_severable(entry), e) })

// A function's own severance ABOVE its module's — the delta, which is the
// only part of its candidate set that is news.
fn severance_beyond(module_sev, sev) with Memory + Alloc =
  sev |> filter({ e => not_in_names(module_sev, e) })

fn not_in_names(names, target: EffName) with Memory + Alloc = !name_in_list(names, target)

// The candidates whose absence buys a NAMED capability — the teaching half.
// The rest are true and carry nothing to act on, so they ride as one count
// at the module, where they describe the capability MAP's gap rather than
// the developer's code.
fn severance_named(sev) with Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  sev |> filter({ e => len(capabilities_for_severance(e)) > 0 })

// Severance candidates: every effect DECLARED in scope that the body
// does not reach — adding `!E` for each is provable and unlocks what
// its capability mapping names. THE VOCABULARY IS A GRAPH READ (the
// selfhood audit's F12, 2026-07-30): three interned literals stood
// here while the env held 76 effect declarations, so the audit could
// never tell a fn it could prove `!Mutate` / `!WASI` / `!Thread` — the
// severances a real-time or sandboxed consumer actually wants — and
// every pure fn got the identical three-name line, a constant where
// §5's felt endpoint asks for a gradient. EffectDeclKind IS the env's
// own "this name is an effect" edge (register_effect_ops draws it);
// reading it live means a newly-declared effect enters the audit by
// construction, and the literal list (with its drift marker) deletes.
fn severance_vocabulary() with EnvRead + Intern + Memory + Alloc = match env_snapshot() {
  Env(bindings) => bindings |> fold(
    [],
    (acc, b) => match b {
      (name, _, _, EffectDeclKind(_)) => {
        // The flat env carries a decl at several layers (pre_register +
        // the main walk); each effect names itself once.
        let e = ENamed(intern_str(name))
        if name_in_list(acc, e) { acc } else { acc ++ [e] }
      },
      _ => acc,
    }
  ),
}

fn severance_candidates(reached) = severance_vocabulary() |> absent_from(reached)

// absent_from — the candidates not present in `present` (a filter over
// the vocabulary; structural == is the membership — the fold-eq, never
// the hand-rolled twin). Iteration-is-topology's first migrated family:
// five index-threaded loops in this section dissolved into
// filter/any/fold, the audit's own tier the ratchet.
fn absent_from(present, candidates) = candidates |> filter((c) => !name_in_list(present, c))

// The pin is load-bearing (the migration's own first red): under the
// Stage Law the datum infers LAST, so the lambda's `x` is free when it
// compiles and a bare `==` word-floors to pointer-eq — EffName records
// mint per call, membership read always-false, and Alloc was offered
// severable on allocating rows (the severance-honest leg caught it).
// One typed operand restores the structural dispatch (either-operand
// law). The migration recipe carries this: a datum-last lambda doing
// ==/arith on the element states the element's type.
fn name_in_list(names, target: EffName) = names |> any((x) => x == target)

// A capability enters ONCE across the whole severed set: IO and
// Network both unlock CSandbox, and the undeduped concat rendered
// "Sandbox (proven no network access)" twice on every audit line
// whose fn severs both (measured). Structural == over the nullary
// capability ADT is the membership; the fold reads its own
// accumulator for the dedup — genuinely a fold, never a map.
fn severance_unlocks(severable) = severable |> fold(
  [],
  (acc, s) => acc ++ (capabilities_for_severance(s) |> filter((c) => !(acc |> any((x) => x == c))))
)

// Terminal renderer over AuditReport records — reads fields by name.
// JSON / IDE-projection renderers are peer functions on the same
// record (one substrate, multiple projections per CLAUDE.md insight 8).
//
// Positional destructure — provable with no type flow, where a
// record field read floors in a map lambda (see build_audit_report).
fn render_audit(entries) = {
  let module_sev = module_severance(entries)
  let fn_lines = entries |> map({
    (fn_name, row_str, severable, referenced_by, pipe_chains, loop_costume, anon_shapes, drift_shapes, pending, tightens) => audit_report_lines(
      fn_name,
      row_str,
      severance_beyond(module_sev, severable),
      referenced_by,
      pipe_chains,
      loop_costume,
      anon_shapes,
      drift_shapes,
      pending,
      tightens
    ),
  }) |> str_concat_all
  "{render_module_severance(module_sev)}{fn_lines}"
}

// The module's own two lines, read once from the intersection above: what
// the whole module severs and what that buys, then the capability map's gap
// — effects every body provably never reaches that no capability names. The
// second line is a statement about the MEDIUM, not about the code, which is
// why it belongs here once and nowhere per function.
fn render_module_severance(module_sev) with Memory + Alloc + Intern + GraphRead = {
  let named = severance_named(module_sev)
  let unnamed = len(module_sev) - len(named)
  let named_line = if len(named) == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "severs module-wide: {show_list(named, show_eff_name, " + ")} — unlocks {show_list(severance_unlocks(named), show_capability, ", ")}\n"
  }
  let unnamed_line = if unnamed == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "  {int_to_str(unnamed)} declared effect(s) sever module-wide with no capability named — naming one unlocks it everywhere\n"
  }
  "{named_line}{unnamed_line}"
}

// The String pins are Intent Boundaries (spec_mangle's law): inside the
// map lambda the splices judged datum-last while the tuple elements were
// still free, and the word floor rendered every audited fn's name and
// row as pointer numerals. The named call anchors the binders.
// One roster pair → its note fragment; the fold's decl home (a lambda
// here would carry the splice's Alloc row nameless — the anonymity
// tier's own conviction class).
fn drift_note_fold(acc, pair) = match pair {
  (shape, n) => if n == 0 { acc } else { "{acc}{int_to_str(n)} {census_label(shape)}; " },
}

fn audit_report_lines(fn_name: String, row_str: String, beyond, referenced_by: [String], pipe_chains, loop_costume, anon_shapes, drift_shapes, pending, tightens) = {
  let header = "{fn_name} : {row_str}\n"
  // Only the DELTA above the module's own severance, and only its teaching
  // half. A fn that severs exactly what its module severs says nothing here,
  // because the module line already said it — and the unnamed remainder is
  // the capability map's gap, reported at the module where it is one fact
  // instead of a per-function number nobody can act on.
  let named_beyond = severance_named(beyond)
  let severance_section = if len(named_beyond) == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "  severs beyond the module: {show_list(named_beyond, show_eff_name, " + ")} — unlocks {show_list(severance_unlocks(named_beyond), show_capability, ", ")}\n"
  }
  let refs_section = if len(referenced_by) == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "  referenced in comments by: {show_list(referenced_by, (n) => n, ", ")}\n"
  }
  // The verb-shape tier: the bindings already draw a `|>` — say so, with
  // the step count (SYNTAX ⌖: the pipe is never optional on a chain).
  let verb_section = if len(pipe_chains) == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "  verb-shape: {show_list(pipe_chains, int_to_str, ", ")}-step let-chain reads as a |> pipe\n"
  }
  // The iteration-shape tier: iteration is TOPOLOGY (SYNTAX's own law —
  // no loop keywords; |> stages, <~ cycles, Iterate handlers, derived
  // folds); a self-call threading an incremented index is the loop in
  // recursion's costume, and a fold/each/iterate stage serves.
  let iter_section = if loop_costume {
    "  iteration-shape: a self-call threads an incremented index — the loop in recursion's costume; a fold/each/iterate stage serves\n"
  } else {
    ""
  }
  // The anonymity tier (Hβ.audit.anonymity-tier): an eta-wrapper hides
  // a name that exists; an effectful lambda hides a row that deserves a
  // decl home. The pure-local lambda is vocabulary and stays silent.
  let anon_section = match anon_shapes {
    (eta_n, rowed_n) => {
      let eta_note =
        if eta_n == 0 { "" } else { "{int_to_str(eta_n)} eta-wrapper(s) — the named fn serves; " }
      let rowed_note = if rowed_n == 0 {
        ""
      } else {
        "{int_to_str(rowed_n)} effectful lambda(s) — a named stage carries the row; "
      }
      if eta_n + rowed_n == 0 {
        ""
      } else {
        "  anonymity: {eta_note}{rowed_note}intent is lossless, name the stage\n"
      }
    },
  }
  // The drift-shape tier (5.6's absorbed modes, read per fn): the
  // roster's census shapes counted within THIS body's subtree — the
  // audit names the costume where it stands; a deliberate specimen's
  // judgment stays the reader's, as the suppression convention set.
  // The notes fold over the roster pairs through drift_note_fold
  // (census_label the one label home), so a newly absorbed mode
  // renders with no edit here.
  let drift_notes = fold("", drift_note_fold, drift_shapes)
  let drift_section = if byte_len(drift_notes) == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "  drift-shape: {drift_notes}the census locates each\n"
  }
  // The banks' tiers — the same facts the frontier ranks, spoken per fn:
  // undischarged proof obligations in this decl's extent, and the
  // judgment's banked tightening with its proven row (the patch mentl
  // tighten authors).
  let pending_section = if len(pending) == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "  pending: {int_to_str(len(pending))} undischarged proof obligation(s) — the field ranks them\n"
  }
  let tighten_section = tightens |> map({
    (declared, proven, _, _, _) => "  tighten: with {show_effrow(declared)} — body proves {show_effrow(proven)} (mentl tighten authors the patch)\n",
  }) |> str_concat_all
  "{header}{severance_section}{refs_section}{verb_section}{iter_section}{anon_section}{drift_section}{pending_section}{tighten_section}"
}

// Query rendering — delegates to query.mn for Question parsing.
// A census site is a NODE, and this line is its projection — `site_address`
// reads the module and the span from the node's own columns at the moment
// of rendering, or names a cell by its handle and reason when it has no
// position. The (module, span) pair this took was a copy made at the walk,
// and a copy is where `tuples:72:1-75:2` came from.
fn render_census_sites(ref sites) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  sites |> map(census_site_line) |> str_concat_all

fn census_site_line(h) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  "\n  at {site_address(h)}"

// The facts that convicted the sites, most frequent first — which declaration
// a count is made of, before the coordinates that make it up.
fn render_census_facts(facts) with Memory + Alloc = facts |> map(census_fact_line) |> str_concat_all

fn census_fact_line(entry) with Memory + Alloc = match entry {
  (fact, n) => "\n  {int_to_str(n)} × {fact}",
}

// A declaration as a reader looks for it: its own name, then where it lives.
// The decls facet rendered the census line here — 1,155 bare addresses and no
// name among them (measured 2026-09-22) — so a roster asked for by name
// answered by coordinate, and every use of it was a second query.
fn decl_named_site(h) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  "{body_decl_name(graph_node_body(h))} at {site_address(h)}"

fn render_decl_sites(sites) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  sites |> map({ h => "\n  {decl_named_site(h)}" }) |> str_concat_all

// The declaring node on its own line ahead of what reads it — nothing for a
// name no source node declared.
fn render_declared_at(decl) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern = match decl {
  Some(h) => "\n  declared at {site_address(h)}",
  None => "",
}

// An authored row as its author wrote it: each term with the connective that
// joins it and its sign — the `with` clause, and a named row's right side.
fn show_row_terms(terms) with GraphRead + Memory + Alloc + Intern = terms |> map({
  (name, negated, conn) => "{show_connective(conn)}{if negated { "!" } else { "" }}{show_eff_name(name)}",
}) |> str_concat_all

fn show_connective(conn) = match conn {
  EcUnion => "+",
  EcDiff => "-",
  EcInter => "&",
}

// Each providing arm by its handler's name, at the arm's own address.
fn render_provider_arms(arms) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  arms |> map({ (h, arm) => "\n  {body_decl_name(graph_node_body(h))} at {site_address(arm)}" }) |> str_concat_all

// The judgment's heaviest decls — bytes of judgment heap each, the decl's
// name read off its handle's body, its address off its columns.
fn render_judged_rows(rows) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  rows |> map(judged_row_line) |> str_concat_all

fn judged_row_line(row: (Int, Int)) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern = match row {
  (h, bytes) => "\n  {bytes} B  {decl_named_site(h)}",
}

// One line per undischarged obligation: the predicate the graph holds,
// at the developer's own coordinates — the debt facet's site list.
// The seam walk is GONE: the span is already the developer's own coordinate
// and the module rides the obligation, so a line is one read and a name, with
// no containment scan over every node to place it.
fn render_debt_lines(obligations) with GraphRead + Memory + Alloc =
  obligations |> map(render_debt_line) |> str_concat_all

fn render_debt_line(ob) with GraphRead + Memory + Alloc = match ob {
  (modh, s, pred, _) => "\n  {show_predicate(pred)} at {module_name_of_handle(modh)}:{show_span(s)}",
}

fn render_smt_lines(obligations) with GraphRead + Memory + Alloc + Diagnostic + Intern =
  obligations |> map(render_smt_line) |> str_concat_all

fn render_smt_line(ob) with GraphRead + Memory + Alloc + Diagnostic + Intern = match ob {
  (modh, s, pred, _) => "\n; {module_name_of_handle(modh)}:{show_span(s)}\n{predicate_to_smt_lib(pred)}",
}

// The import edges rendered as a verdict per edge. DEAD means the imported
// module brings no name this one references — measured off the refs column,
// not guessed from text, which is the whole reason the facet exists: a grep
// cannot tell a used name from one mentioned in a comment, and 52 of these
// sat unseen behind exactly that.
fn render_import_row(row) with Pure = match row {
  (m, imported, used) => {
    let mark = if used { "used" } else { "DEAD" }
    "  {mark}  {m} -> import {imported}"
  },
}

fn import_row_is_dead(row) with Pure = match row {
  (_, _, used) => !used,
}

fn render_import_rows(rows) with Memory + Alloc =
  "→ {int_to_str(len(rows))} import edge(s); {int_to_str(count(import_row_is_dead, rows))} bring nothing the importing module references\n{str_join_indented(map(render_import_row, rows))}"

// The declared names rendered as the roster's dead half. The header states
// the whole roster so the count reads against it; the body names only what
// nothing outside its own declaration reaches. UNREFERENCED is not
// unreachable — it is the direct reference, measured, and a name reached
// through an edge the graph does not draw surfaces here as exactly that
// finding, never as noise to tune away.
fn render_unref_row(row) with Pure = match row {
  (m, name, _) => "  UNREFERENCED  {m} -> {name}",
}

fn unref_row_is_dead(row) with Pure = match row {
  (_, _, outside) => outside == 0,
}

// The transitive face: a row's third field is reached-from-entry, so the
// same zero test names the fns the entry cannot reach.
// THE FACET ANSWERED TWO DIFFERENT QUESTIONS IN ONE FLAT LIST, and the
// measurement is why it is split. `mentl src/main.mn unreachable`
// answered 276 fn decls, and 202 of them sat in modules where NOTHING is
// reached — prelude, combinators, dsp/*, ml/*, math, lists, strings: the
// library surface a program LINKS and does not call, which is not dead code
// and never was. The other 74 sat inside modules the entry runs through every
// time, which IS dead code and is the whole finding. Handed one list of 276,
// a reader acts on neither.
//
// The distinguishing fact is a RATIO this walk already holds. A module whose
// unreached count equals its total is surface; a module with reached decls
// standing beside unreached ones is carrying weight. No path convention
// decides it — not `src/` versus `lib/`, which is a directory habit the graph
// knows nothing about — the reachability walk does, from edges it already has.
fn render_unreach_rows(rows) with Memory + Alloc = {
  let groups = unreach_groups(rows)
  let carrying = groups |> filter(group_carries_dead)
  let surface = groups |> filter(group_is_surface)
  let dead_n = count(unref_row_is_dead, rows)
  let header = "→ {int_to_str(len(rows))} fn decl(s); {int_to_str(dead_n)} the entry cannot reach\n"
  let carrying_section = if len(carrying) == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "\nDEAD — in modules the entry reaches:\n{carrying |> map(render_carrying_group) |> str_concat_all}"
  }
  let surface_section = if len(surface) == 0 {
    ""
  } else {
    "\nSURFACE — {int_to_str(len(surface))} module(s) linked whole and never called into:\n{surface |> map(render_surface_group) |> str_concat_all}"
  }
  "{header}{carrying_section}{surface_section}"
}

// Each line arrives whole, newline included, and concatenates — never through
// `str_join_indented`, which is for flat rows under one header. Over a nested
// render its two-space step compounds: the module rows printed at 2, 4, 4 and
// their decls at 6, 8, 8, which is what the first run of this projection did
// and what renamed that helper.
fn render_carrying_group(g) with Memory + Alloc = match g {
  (m, total, dead) => "  {m} — {int_to_str(len(dead))} of {int_to_str(total)} unreached\n{dead |> map(render_unreach_name) |> str_concat_all}",
}

fn render_unreach_name(name: String) with Memory + Alloc = "      {name}\n"

fn render_surface_group(g) with Memory + Alloc = match g {
  (m, total, _) => "  {m} — all {int_to_str(total)}\n",
}

// One pass over the rows, which arrive in module order because the cells do.
// `last` / `drop_last` are the snoc end's O(1) reads, so extending the open
// group costs nothing per row (SYNTAX §Vocabulary — the names say which end).
fn unreach_groups(rows) with Memory + Alloc = rows |> fold([], unreach_group_add)

fn unreach_group_add(acc, row) with Memory + Alloc = match row {
  (m, name, hit) => if len(acc) == 0 {
    [(m, 1, unreach_dead_one(name, hit))]
  } else {
    match last(acc) {
      (gm, total, dead) => if same_module_path(gm, m) {
        drop_last(acc) ++ [(gm, total + 1, dead ++ unreach_dead_one(name, hit))]
      } else {
        acc ++ [(m, 1, unreach_dead_one(name, hit))]
      },
    }
  },
}

// The `: String` pins are the Intent Boundary the either-operand law asks
// for: both operands arrive free out of a tuple destructure, and a bare `==`
// on an unproven operand word-floors to pointer-eq — every group would open
// fresh and the roster would read one module per decl.
fn same_module_path(a: String, b: String) with Memory + Alloc = a == b

fn unreach_dead_one(name, hit) with Memory + Alloc = if hit == 0 { [name] } else { [] }

fn group_carries_dead(g) with Memory + Alloc = match g {
  (_, total, dead) => len(dead) > 0 && len(dead) < total,
}

fn group_is_surface(g) with Memory + Alloc = match g {
  (_, total, dead) => len(dead) > 0 && len(dead) == total,
}

fn render_unref_rows(rows) with Memory + Alloc =
  "→ {int_to_str(len(rows))} declared name(s); {int_to_str(count(unref_row_is_dead, rows))} that nothing outside their own declaration references\n{str_join_indented(map(render_unref_row, filter(unref_row_is_dead, rows)))}"

// Each effect with how many of its ops anything performs. A handler ARM is
// not a perform — it is the promise's other half — so k/n reads as "how
// much of this surface is actually reached." WHOLE is the quiet case; the
// body names only the rest, because a surface at k<n is either half built,
// bypassed at its callers, or dead with its handler still installed, and
// those three are the finds of the last three landings.
fn render_perform_row(row) with Memory + Alloc = match row {
  (m, name, total, done) => {
    let mark = if done == 0 { "NONE" } else { "PART" }
    "  {mark}  {m} -> {name}  {int_to_str(done)}/{int_to_str(total)} ops performed"
  },
}

fn perform_row_is_partial(row) with Pure = match row {
  (_, _, total, done) => done < total,
}

fn render_perform_rows(rows) with Memory + Alloc =
  "→ {int_to_str(len(rows))} effect(s); {int_to_str(count(perform_row_is_partial, rows))} with ops nothing performs\n{str_join_indented(map(render_perform_row, filter(perform_row_is_partial, rows)))}"

// A declaration nothing references, carrying prose that explains how it is
// used. The bytes are the weight of the belief; the zero is the graph
// disagreeing with it. Read the prose to decide — this names the sites, it
// does not judge them.
fn render_orphan_row(row) with Memory + Alloc = match row {
  (m, name, bytes) => "  CLAIMED  {m} -> {name}  ({int_to_str(bytes)} bytes of prose, 0 references)",
}

fn render_orphan_rows(rows) with Memory + Alloc =
  "→ {int_to_str(len(rows))} declaration(s) explained at length and referenced by nothing\n{str_join_indented(map(render_orphan_row, rows))}"

fn render_query_result(result) = match result {
  QRType(ty, reason) => "→ {show_type(ty)}\n  Reason: {show_reason(reason)}",
  QRIntent(effs) => "→ {show_row_terms(effs)}",
  QRUnresolved(entries) => "→ {int_to_str(len(entries))} unresolved entries",
  QRChain(hops) => "→ {int_to_str(len(hops))} hops in chain",
  QREffects(row) => "→ {show_effrow(row)}",
  QRRow(present, absent, tail) => // The row as the algebra holds it: every name beside the intern handle
  // `eff_name_handle` keys on, so a reader can see whether two names that
  // SPELL alike also KEY alike. `effects` renders the spelling; this renders
  // the comparison, which is the half a set union is decided by.
  "→ present {int_to_str(len(present))}: {show_keyed_names(present, 0, len(present), "")}\n  absent {int_to_str(len(absent))}: {show_keyed_names(absent, 0, len(absent), "")}\n  tail {tail}",
  QROwnership(params) => "→ {int_to_str(len(params))} params",
  QRWhy(reason) => // A declared name's chain ends at the edge to its declaring node, and
  // show_reason renders that node's own address. It rendered a Located span
  // with no module until the reason carried the node — `why
  // unify_row_canonical` on a linked program answered `at 867:1-963:2` and
  // left the reader to guess the file (measured 2026-09-22).
  "→ {show_reason(reason)}",
  QRRefs(decl, sites) => // The refs facet renders WHAT the graph computed, not just how much:
  // one located line per inbound use-edge (the seam the propose-facet fix
  // convicted once already — the graph computed it, the terminal threw it
  // away). Every "who calls X" grep this replaces was a re-derivation of
  // edges the weave holds — and the answer is only a replacement once it
  // names the FILE, which is why it renders through the census's own site
  // line rather than a second renderer that knew one half of an address.
  // The declaration leads: this is a rename's edit set, and a set without
  // the declaring node renames every use and leaves the name itself behind.
  "→ {int_to_str(len(sites))} reference(s){render_declared_at(decl)}{render_census_sites(sites)}",
  QRVerifyDebt(obligations) => // The debt renders WHAT is owed, not just how much (the refs facet's
  // own lesson): each obligation located with its predicate, so the
  // discharge work has an instrument instead of a count.
  "→ {int_to_str(len(obligations))} verification obligations pending{render_debt_lines(obligations)}",
  QRSmt(obligations) => // The same obligations in the solver's language, each assertion located
  // so a discharged one can be walked back to the claim that raised it.
  // `predicate_to_smt_lib` is verify.mn's own serializer — this render is
  // its first reader, and Phase 8.3's handler swap is its second.
  "→ {int_to_str(len(obligations))} obligation(s) as SMT-LIB{render_smt_lines(obligations)}",
  QRHandlerProvider(arms) => if len(arms) == 0 {
    "→ no handler declaration provides it"
  } else {
    "→ handled at {int_to_str(len(arms))} arm(s){render_provider_arms(arms)}"
  },
  QRFlowLabel(label, reason) => "→ {show_flow_label(label)}\n  Reason: {show_reason(reason)}",
  QRCensus(label, sites, facts) => "→ {int_to_str(len(sites))} {label}{render_census_facts(facts)}{render_census_sites(sites)}",
  QRDecls(sites) => // The decls column's projection, each declaration by its own name and
  // its address — the roster a reader navigates by.
  "→ {int_to_str(len(sites))} declaration(s){render_decl_sites(sites)}",
  QRModules(paths) => "→ {int_to_str(len(paths))} module(s) in the weave\n  {str_join_indented(paths)}",
  QRImports(rows) => render_import_rows(rows),
  QRUnreferenced(rows) => render_unref_rows(rows),
  QRUnreachable(rows) => render_unreach_rows(rows),
  QRPerforms(rows) => render_perform_rows(rows),
  QROrphanClaims(rows) => render_orphan_rows(rows),
  QRCost(mods, lines, nodes, judged) => "→ {int_to_str(mods)} module(s) · {int_to_str(lines)} source line(s) · {int_to_str(nodes)} node(s) minted{render_judged_rows(judged)}",
  QRWhere(lines, sites) => "→ {str_join_indented(lines)}{render_where_sites(sites)}",
  QRError(msg) => "error: {msg}",
}

// It JOINS AND INDENTS — every element after the first lands two spaces in —
// and the name said only the first half until a nested render read as a
// staircase (module rows at 2, 4, 4; their decls at 6, 8, 8). A helper whose
// name hides half of what it does is the representation lying, one layer up
// from the list_head/list_tail pair that read the snoc end until `last` and
// `drop_last` replaced them (SYNTAX §Vocabulary). The callers
// that want the indent name it; a caller that wants whole lines concatenates
// them itself.
fn str_join_indented(lines) with Pure = match lines {
  [] => "",
  [one] => one,
  [h, ...t] => "{h}\n  {str_join_indented(t)}",
}

// The site badges: the schedule word at the fanout's own line —
// `>< [Thread] at file:line` — the exact fact lower reads ambiently,
// projected statically (the where stamp's exactness law).
fn render_where_sites(sites) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern = match sites {
  [] => "",
  [(word, h), ...t] => "\n  >< [{word}] at {site_address(h)}{render_where_sites(t)}",
}

// show_flow_label — defined in types.mn alongside flow_label_join/flow_le.
//
// The query surface is a tiny grammar: <verb> [arg]. The query strings are
// unavoidable external input (like LSP method strings, lsp.mn classify_method)
// — projected to the QueryVerb ADT at ONE boundary (classify_query_verb),
// downstream ADT-only. build_question reads the verb structurally and pairs it
// with its argument arity; no nested string-literal cascade scattered across
// arities (drift 8). An ill-formed query is QUnknown(q) — the honest Silence,
// never a fabricated Question.
type QueryVerb
  = QVType
  | QVEffects
  | QVRow
  | QVOwnership
  | QVWhy
  | QVRefs
  | QVProvider
  | QVUnresolved
  | QVVerification
  | QVFlow
  | QVCensus
  | QVWhere
  | QVDecls
  | QVVariants
  | QVModules
  | QVImports
  | QVUnreferenced
  | QVUnreachable
  | QVPerforms
  | QVOrphanClaims
  | QVCost
  | QVSmt
  | QVUnknownVerb

// One name beside its key, repeated — `Memory#41` reads as the pair it is.
fn show_keyed_names(ns, i, n, acc: String) with Memory + Alloc = if i >= n {
  acc
} else {
  match list_index(ns, i) {
    (spelling, handle) => show_keyed_names(ns, i + 1, n, "{acc}{if i > 0 { " " } else { "" }}{spelling}#{int_to_str(handle)}"),
  }
}

fn classify_query_verb(w: String) with Pure = if w == "type" {
  QVType
} else if w == "effects" {
  QVEffects
} else if w == "row" {
  QVRow
} else if w == "ownership" {
  QVOwnership
} else if w == "why" {
  QVWhy
} else if w == "refs" {
  QVRefs
} else if w == "provider" {
  QVProvider
} else if w == "unresolved" {
  QVUnresolved
} else if w == "verification" {
  QVVerification
} else if w == "flow" {
  QVFlow
} else if w == "census" {
  QVCensus
} else if w == "where" {
  QVWhere
} else if w == "decls" {
  QVDecls
} else if w == "variants" {
  QVVariants
} else if w == "modules" {
  QVModules
} else if w == "imports" {
  QVImports
} else if w == "unreferenced" {
  QVUnreferenced
} else if w == "unreachable" {
  QVUnreachable
} else if w == "performs" {
  QVPerforms
} else if w == "orphan-claims" {
  QVOrphanClaims
} else if w == "cost" {
  QVCost
} else if w == "smt" {
  QVSmt
} else {
  QVUnknownVerb
}

// The grammar reads WORDS, because that is what a question is. The terminal
// hands them already split (`mentl src/infer.mn why unify` — argv IS the
// split), so the CLI no longer joins them for this fn to split again.
fn parse_query_words(ws) = {
  // A caller's list may be a slice VIEW; the list-pattern match assumes the
  // flat [len][elems] contract, so flatten once before matching (§7 face 13)
  // — and read words ONCE, never re-split per arm (Carried-Truth).
  let words = list_to_flat(ws)
  match words {
    [] => QUnknown(""),
    [w0] => build_question(classify_query_verb(w0), "", words),
    [w0, w1] => build_question(classify_query_verb(w0), w1, words),
    _ => build_question(classify_query_verb(query_head(words)), query_last(words), words),
  }
}

// The adapter for a transport whose question genuinely arrives as ONE string:
// the MCP wire carries a line, so the split happens once, here, at that
// boundary. `parse_query_words` stays the grammar's one home.
fn parse_query_string(q) with Memory + Alloc = parse_query_words(split(" ", q))

// build_question — pair the classified verb with its argument. Nullary verbs
// (unresolved/verification) ignore the arg; unary verbs carry it. A verb whose
// arity its arg cannot satisfy projects to QUnknown(raw) — the honest unknown.
// `raw` is the question's WORDS, re-joined only to be READ BACK to the person
// who asked: the byte-sequence survives as a display projection, never as the
// carrier (`PLAN.md §5.O` — a name's ultimate representation is a word).
fn build_question(verb, arg, words) with Memory + Alloc = {
  let raw = join(" ", list_to_flat(words))
  match verb {
    QVUnresolved => QUnresolved,
    QVVerification => QVerifyDebt,
    QVType => QTypeOf(arg),
    QVEffects => QEffects(arg),
    QVRow => QRowOf(arg),
    QVOwnership => QOwnership(arg),
    QVWhy => QWhy(arg),
    QVRefs => QRefsOf(arg),
    QVProvider => QHandlerProvider(arg),
    QVFlow => QFlowOf(arg),
    QVCensus => match census_shape_of(arg) {
      Some(shape) => QCensus(shape),
      None => QUnknown(raw),
    },
    QVWhere => QWhere(arg),
    QVDecls => QDecls,
    QVVariants => QVariants(arg),
    QVModules => QModules,
    QVImports => QImports,
    QVUnreferenced => QUnreferenced,
    QVUnreachable => QUnreachable,
    QVPerforms => QPerforms,
    QVOrphanClaims => QOrphanClaims,
    QVCost => QCost,
    QVSmt => QSmt,
    QVUnknownVerb => QUnknown(raw),
  }
}

// The shape classifier at the grammar's one boundary: a named judgment
// shape, "anonymous", or one of the five glyphs matched THROUGH
// show_pipe_kind (the one glyph projection — the constructor roster
// appears exactly here, where the external string enters). An
// unrecognized shape is the honest QUnknown.
fn census_shape_of(arg) with Memory + Alloc = if arg == "anonymous" {
  Some(CsAnonymous)
} else if arg == "eta" {
  Some(CsEta)
} else if arg == "effectful-lambda" {
  Some(CsEffectfulLambda)
} else if arg == "iteration" {
  Some(CsIterationCostume)
} else if arg == "wildcard-zero" {
  Some(CsWildcardZero)
} else if arg == "failure-mask" {
  Some(CsFailureMask)
} else if arg == "print-in-report" {
  Some(CsPrintInReport)
} else if arg == "wildcard-fabricates" {
  Some(CsWildcardFabricates)
} else if arg == "underscore-retain" {
  Some(CsUnderscoreRetain)
} else if arg == "flag-as-int" {
  Some(CsFlagAsInt)
} else if arg == "parallel-arrays" {
  Some(CsParallelArrays)
} else if arg == "vtable-record" {
  Some(CsVtableRecord)
} else if arg == "env-frame" {
  Some(CsEnvFrame)
} else if arg == "default-param" {
  Some(CsDefaultParam)
} else if arg == "declared-row-hof" {
  Some(CsDeclaredRowHof)
} else if arg == "wide-row" {
  Some(CsWideRow)
} else if arg == "record-pattern" {
  Some(CsRecordPattern)
} else if arg == "record-pattern-open" {
  Some(CsRecordPatternOpen)
} else if arg == "free-row-callee" {
  Some(CsFreeRowCallee)
} else if arg == "free-row-var" {
  Some(CsFreeRowVar)
} else if arg == "audit-silenced" {
  Some(CsAuditSilenced)
} else if arg == "wildcard-destructure" {
  Some(CsWildcardDestructure)
} else {
  match find(
    (k) => show_pipe_kind(k) == arg,
    [PForward, PFanout(FanShare), PFanout(FanDistribute), PTee, PFeedback]
  ) {
    Some(k) => Some(CsVerb(k)),
    None => None,
  }
}

// The verb is the FIRST word (`<verb> [arg]` — the documented query
// grammar); the prior read of last(ws) made every 3+-word query's verb
// and argument the SAME final word.
fn query_head(ws) with Memory = if len(ws) == 0 { "" } else { head(ws) }

fn query_last(ws) with Memory = if len(ws) == 0 { "" } else { list_index(ws, len(ws) - 1) }
